\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O word of God incarnate,
\par O Wisdom from on high,
\par O Truth unchanged, unchanging,
\par O Light of our dark sky,
\par We praise Thee for the radiance
\par That from the hallowed page,
\par A lantern to our footsteps,
\par Shines on from age to age.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The Church from her dear Master
\par Received the gift divine,
\par And still that light she lifteth,
\par O'er all the earth to shine;
\par It is the golden casket
\par Where gems of truth are stored;
\par It is the heaven-drawn picture
\par Of Christ, the living Word;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. It floateth like a banner
\par Before God's host unfurled;
\par It shineth like a beacon
\par Above the darkling world;
\par It is the chart and compass
\par That, o'er life's surging sea,
\par Mid mists, and rocks, and quicksands,
\par Still guides, O Christ, to Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O make Thy Church, dear Saviour,
\par A lamb of burnished gold,
\par To bear before the nations
\par Thy true light, as of old;
\par O teach Thy wandering pilgrims
\par By this their path to trace,
\par Till, clouds and darkness ended,
\par They see Thee face to face.\f1 
\par 
\par }

